Description:
    Provides an automated, reproducible pipeline for gating multi-colour flow
    cytometry data stored in FCS files.  Starting from raw FCS data, the
    package applies spectral compensation and biexponential transformation,
    then executes a user-defined sequence of population gates (singlets,
    leukocytes, lineage sub-populations) followed by activation marker gates.
    Gate boundaries are calculated automatically from the data using one of
    four threshold algorithms — symmetric tail probability, bimodal valley
    detection, Gaussian mixture model crossover, or KDE local minimum — or
    can be replicated from a previously calculated gate.  All gates are
    visualised as density-coloured scatter plots with labelled population
    boundaries, and population fractions together with activation marker
    expression statistics (fraction positive, median, IQR) are exported as
    tidy CSV files.  Instrument-specific parameter profiles are provided for
    the BD FACSymphony, Cytek Aurora, and Sony ID7000 cytometers, and new
    profiles can be added by implementing a single parameter-override function.
